# Data & Network Integration (Core)

All HTTP calls use **Ktor Client** with the project **`ApiRequest`** wrapper (reference: `data/auth`).

## ApiRequest Definition

```kotlin
internal object AuthApi {
    fun getLogin(request: LoginRequest) = ApiRequest<LoginResponse>(
        url = ApiConstants.BASE_URL,
        method = ApiMethod.POST,
        path = "/ZWFM_FM_GET_USER",
        requestBody = request
    )
}
```

## Data Sources

| Type | Responsibility |
|------|----------------|
| `RemoteDataSource` | Pass `ApiRequest` objects to Ktor |
| `LocalDataSource` | Room / SQLDelight reads and writes |

## Repository (Single Source of Truth)

```kotlin
// ❌ BAD — UseCase calls data source directly
class GetCategoriesUseCase(private val remote: CategoryRemoteDataSource)

// ✅ GOOD — RepositoryImpl merges sources
// fetch remote → persist local → read local → return to UseCase
class CategoryRepositoryImpl(
    private val remote: CategoryRemoteDataSource,
    private val local: CategoryLocalDataSource,
) : CategoryRepository
```

UseCases must **never** call DataSources directly — only Repository interfaces.
